{%- comment -%}
  Details / Size & fit / Fabric & care / Shipping — port of
  components/product/product-tabs.tsx, plus the size-and-fit panel the brief
  asks for (§11: size chart, fit information).

  Real ARIA tabs, which means the keyboard contract has to be real too: arrow keys
  move between tabs, Home and End jump to the ends, and the tab strip is a single
  tab stop with Tab moving on to the panel. A row of buttons that only responds to
  clicks looks like this and is not this. See wl-tabs in assets/theme.js.

  A panel whose copy has not been written renders the labelled placeholder at body
  size, so the block keeps its height either way. Details comes from the product
  description and Fabric & care from a `custom.care` metafield; both are blank on
  this catalogue on purpose — the design reused one generic paragraph for all
  eleven pieces, which would state a wrong inseam and a wrong fabric on most of
  them.

  SIZE & FIT IS THE SECOND TAB, not the last. Two things put it there and they
  agree: the brief lists size chart and fit information ahead of care
  instructions, and PRODUCT.md records fit as the purchase decision itself —
  almost every one of the twenty customer reviews names a height and a weight
  before it names a size. The tab a shopper needs first is the one next to
  Details. Reordering it later is a change to what the page prioritises, not a
  tidy-up.

  Its two halves are separate metafields on purpose. A size chart is tabular and
  a fit note is prose; one rich-text field holding both means the studio has to
  remember the shape as well as the content. Each renders its own labelled
  placeholder, so a product with a chart but no fit note shows exactly that.

  Without JavaScript every panel is visible in sequence and the tab strip is
  removed, rather than two panels of copy being lost to a control that cannot
  work — see the `scripting: none` block in theme-src/theme.css. The copy is the
  point; the tabbing is the enhancement.

  Accepts: product, shipping (store-wide policy copy)
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="border-t border-rule" data-tabs>
  <div role="tablist" class="flex flex-wrap">
    <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-details" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="panel-details" tabindex="0"
      class="wl-press-soft cursor-pointer border-b-2 border-transparent px-6 py-5.5 text-label uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-subtle transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) hover:text-brand aria-selected:border-brand aria-selected:text-ink sm:px-8">
      {{ 'product.details' | t }}
    </button>
    <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-fit" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-fit" tabindex="-1"
      class="wl-press-soft cursor-pointer border-b-2 border-transparent px-6 py-5.5 text-label uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-subtle transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) hover:text-brand aria-selected:border-brand aria-selected:text-ink sm:px-8">
      {{ 'product.size_and_fit' | t }}
    </button>
    <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-care" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-care" tabindex="-1"
      class="wl-press-soft cursor-pointer border-b-2 border-transparent px-6 py-5.5 text-label uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-subtle transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) hover:text-brand aria-selected:border-brand aria-selected:text-ink sm:px-8">
      {{ 'product.fabric_and_care' | t }}
    </button>
    <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-shipping" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-shipping" tabindex="-1"
      class="wl-press-soft cursor-pointer border-b-2 border-transparent px-6 py-5.5 text-label uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-subtle transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) hover:text-brand aria-selected:border-brand aria-selected:text-ink sm:px-8">
      {{ 'product.shipping' | t }}
    </button>
  </div>

  <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-details" aria-labelledby="tab-details" tabindex="0"
    class="wl-measure py-8 text-body leading-body text-ink-body">
    {% render 'copy', value: product.description, label: 'product details', lines: 3 %}
  </div>

  <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-fit" aria-labelledby="tab-fit" tabindex="0" data-tab-hidden
    class="wl-measure flex flex-col gap-7 py-8 text-body leading-body text-ink-body">
    {%- comment -%}
      `wl-table` in theme-src/theme.css is what makes a size chart pasted into a
      rich-text metafield readable: Shopify emits a bare <table>, and base.css
      styles nothing inside one. It also scrolls sideways rather than forcing the
      column wider than the phone it is on.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h3 class="text-micro uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-subtle">{{ 'product.size_chart' | t }}</h3>
      <div class="wl-table">
        {% render 'copy', value: product.metafields.custom.size_chart.value, label: 'size chart', lines: 4 %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h3 class="text-micro uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-subtle">{{ 'product.fit_information' | t }}</h3>
      {% render 'copy', value: product.metafields.custom.fit.value, label: 'fit information', lines: 2 %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-care" aria-labelledby="tab-care" tabindex="0" data-tab-hidden
    class="wl-measure py-8 text-body leading-body text-ink-body">
    {% render 'copy', value: product.metafields.custom.care.value, label: 'fabric and care', lines: 3 %}
  </div>

  <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-shipping" aria-labelledby="tab-shipping" tabindex="0" data-tab-hidden
    class="wl-measure py-8 text-body leading-body text-ink-body">
    {% render 'copy', value: shipping, label: 'shipping', lines: 3 %}
  </div>
</div>
